        (kind: Loot(table: "driver_cache"), at: (46.4, -133.7), name: "Driver's cache"),
        // notes:begin (generated by scripts/place_notes.py)
        (kind: Note(text: "SOUTH GATE - DUTY LOG, 14 OCT\n0600. Buses out of the depot, 9 of 9.\n0655. Bus 4 back, empty. Driver asks to go in for his mother. Refused.\n0710. Driver still here. Refused again. Escorted to the road.\n1300. A dog barking in the village all afternoon.\n2200. Lights by the well. Not ours."), at: (29.2, 163.8), rot: 63.4, name: "Gate log"),
        (kind: Note(text: "Anna -\nThey said three days. That was three weeks ago. Lev drove the four and wouldn't look at me, so I stayed for the dog.\nThe white machines came out of the new Gate this morning and started tidying. They took the bins. They took the bicycles. They took Mr Holm.\nKeep still when the little flying one looks at you. It sees you move.\nTell Lev I'm not angry. I've written to him as well, for when he comes.\n- Mum"), at: (-19.6, 62.2), rot: 208.3, name: "Village note"),
        (kind: Note(text: "POST OFFICE - UNDELIVERED\nTo O. Vey, station chief, Hollow survey post.\nYour lockbox holds the depot key for Marrow (KEY-M). It is to stay with you. Do not leave it at the post. The Authority will collect all three keys at the review.\nP. Rus, Inspector Quarantine Authority, valley office, 20 Nov."), at: (-21.4, 31.8), rot: 205.2, name: "Post office letter"),
        (kind: Note(text: "CREDIT BOOK\nHolm - bread, paraffin. 3.40\nSedlak - batteries x6, lamp oil. 5.10\nMarek H. - bread, dog biscuits x4, tea. 2.80\nBrabec - nails, tea. 1.95\nVey (survey) - batteries x12, chalk. Paid.\n13 Oct. Shut till further notice. Pay me when you're back."), at: (-17.9, 1.9), rot: 194.0, name: "Credit book"),
        (kind: Note(text: "Walkers:\nDon't waste rounds on the shell. The eye under the front plate, or the knees. They go down like a felled tree.\nThe flyers are glass and wire. One good hit.\nAnd never shoot near the well. It doesn't like it.\n- J., logging camp"), at: (-110.5, 114.1), rot: 331.4, name: "Foreman's note"),
        (kind: Note(text: "PUMP LOG - O. Brabec\nThe Authority says the Surge is theirs: \"scheduled discharge\". It was here first. 9 Oct, before any machine, the sky went the colour of a bruise and every needle in this station lay down.\nThe well in the village takes what you give it. Sometimes it gives back: a quiet hour, a word about where the stones are.\nMy grandmother fed it bread. It was slower then.\nDon't give it your gun."), at: (-104.2, 9.1), rot: 242.7, name: "Pump station note"),
        (kind: Terminal(pages: ["QUARANTINE AUTHORITY\nCUSTODIAN NETWORK - MARROW\n\nDepot GATE-M: ACTIVE\nMode: SWEEP\nUnits: survey, haul, build,\n       recover\n\nThe Custodian keeps the valley\nclean until the review.", "KEPT PENDING REVIEW\n\nBuses                  9\nBicycles             212\nRefuse bins          340\nDomestic animals      58\nPersonnel             31\n\nCondition: kept.", "DEPOT ACCESS\n\nThe depots answer only to the\nAuthority. Recall needs the\nthree valley keys, presented\ntogether at any depot lock:\n\n  KEY-M  Marrow  (Hollow post)\n  KEY-K  Kettle  (quarry)\n  KEY-C  Cinder  (the works)", "REVIEW STATUS\n\nReview date: 1 APR (postponed)\nReview date: (not set)\nAuthority staff on site: 0\nLast login: P.RUS (Cinder)\n\nCustodian continues SWEEP until\nrecalled."]), at: (26.0, -110.5), rot: 118.0, name: "Depot office terminal"),
        (kind: Terminal(pages: ["RELAY LOG - MAST M1\n\nPylons extend the Custodian's\neyes: each one reports what\nmoves near it, and the depot\nsends a team.\n\nPylon down = reports stop.", "SWEEP SCHEDULE\n\nField discharge (\"SURGE\") every\ncycle. Clears contamination.\nPersonnel: be under a roof or\nout of the valley. Loose\nmaterial is reset.\n\nSchedule source: OBSERVED."]), at: (-46.0, -62.1), rot: -179.7, name: "Mast terminal"),
        (kind: Note(text: "SURVEY POST - HOLLOW\n21 Nov. Ground up 41 cm since spring. The glow is brighter the nights before a discharge; I can predict them now. Nobody at the Authority wants to hear it.\nThe inspector's letter never came, but I know what the lockbox is for. Nobody else is going to keep it.\nGoing down at first light to read the centre stakes. Taking the box.\n- O.V."), at: (36.0, 15.6), rot: 328.6, y: 8.5, name: "Survey log"),
        (kind: Note(text: "From up here you can see the Hollow glow after dark. The survey team went in with the chief's lockbox and came back without the chief. The box is still down there, where the ground lifts. Bring a light. Don't run.\nLamp to Kettle tower, 2100: no answer from Emil three nights now.\n- M. Sedlak"), at: (-151.3, -91.4), rot: 333.4, y: 8.5, name: "Ranger's note"),
        (kind: Note(text: "Crew tally, on the wall by the bed:\nMon 14 logs Tue 16 Wed 15 Thu - buses\nThere's a tin of beans under the bed for whoever's next. Wedge the door at night with the split log, the latch is no good.\n- Tomas, J.'s crew"), at: (-71.1, 113.0), rot: 151.4, name: "Cabin tally"),
        // notes:end
    ],

